// `int128` addition past 2^127−1 must trap, at every optimization level.
//
// The level matters more than the trap. The optimizer's constant folder computes
// `max + 1` while folding, and if it does that with a bare `a + b` the result wraps
// to −2^127 -- which is *inside* `int128`, so the range check approves it and the
// folder deletes the instruction that would have trapped. The program then prints a
// number where O0 raises an error. Same source, different answers.

function main():void {
    int128 maxv = 170141183460469231731687303715884105727i128;
    int128 one = 1;
    print("before\n");
    int128 boom = maxv + one;
    print(boom);
    eof: pass;
}
